TidaLunar - Linux .tar.gz package
==================================

Quick start:
  tar -xzf {BUNDLE}.tar.gz
  cd {BUNDLE}/
  ./tidalunar

Sandbox status
==============
This .tar.gz package ships the Chromium sandbox helper without the setuid
bit: an archive you extract as a user cannot set it.
Depending on your distro, TidaLunar will run with one of:

  * Namespace sandbox (Debian 12+, Fedora 39+, Arch, openSUSE Leap 15.5+,
    Linux Mint 22, Ubuntu 22.04) -- sandboxing active.
  * Seccomp-only or no sandbox (Ubuntu 24.04+ with default kernel
    hardening, or kernels without unprivileged user namespaces) --
    reduced sandboxing.

If you want the full Chromium sandbox on Ubuntu 24.04+, install the .deb
package instead:

  sudo apt install ./{DEB}

The .deb ships a sandbox helper (made setuid when the kernel restricts
unprivileged user namespaces), an AppArmor profile, and an install-time
check that picks the mode.

Updates
=======
TidaLunar looks for a new version when it starts; the setting "Auto-check on
startup" turns that off. Nothing is downloaded until you click Update (or
Download, in the settings). The download goes into the folder you extracted,
and the app restarts into the new version when you click "Apply & Restart".
That folder is the installation: keep it, and keep it writable by your user,
since updates are downloaded and installed inside it. Settings, cache and
logs live in ~/.local/share/tidalunar/. The .tar.gz you downloaded is not
used after extraction; you can delete it.
